prompt:
`count_down(int n)` never terminates for n <= 0 and the loop's counter never reaches its bound for n = 5 (it stops early only by luck of the bug). Fix it to return the number of steps counting n, n-1, ..., 1 (so count_down(5) is 5; count_down(0) is 0).

```c
int count_down(int n) {
    int steps = 0;
    while (n != 1) {
        steps++;
        n = n - 0;   /* BUG */
    }
    return steps;
}
```
